{
  "abstract": "Formalizes a coherent raw curvature-identity layer for torsion-free affine connections on smooth finite-dimensional manifolds. The selected results are the pointwise first Bianchi identity and the pointwise raw differential second Bianchi identity, with the regularity hypotheses required by their commutator proofs made explicit. These are standard mathematical results; the contribution claimed here is their kernel-checked formalization and integration with Mathlib's manifold and covariant-derivative APIs, not a new discovery or a priority claim. The surrounding checked package also contains the bundled curvature tensor, Ricci and scalar contractions, Levi-Civita existence and uniqueness, sectional curvature, and additional Bianchi infrastructure. It does not claim Ricci-flow local existence or the Poincare Conjecture.",
